.TH heliosctl-wifi 1 0.5.0 "heliosctl 0.5.0" "Helios Manual"
.SH NAME
heliosctl\-wifi \- The Wi\-Fi networks a device joins: list, set, remove
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBheliosctl wifi\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-show\-secrets\fR] [\fB\-\-endpoint\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-region\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Wi\-Fi networks a device joins: list, set, remove
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON document on stdout, and errors as JSON on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-secrets\fR
Show secrets in full: destinations\*(Aq and Wi\-Fi networks\*(Aq passphrases (else `***`)
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fI<ENDPOINT>\fR
The Control API\*(Aqs base URL (…/dev)
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
The AWS profile: one that assumes helios\-operator [default: helios\-operator]
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR \fI<REGION>\fR
The AWS region [default: the profile\*(Aqs]
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
heliosctl\-wifi\-list(1)
The Wi\-Fi networks the device is set to join (passphrases as *** unless \-\-show\-secrets)
.TP
heliosctl\-wifi\-set(1)
Add a network, or change one: the device applies it before this returns
.TP
heliosctl\-wifi\-remove(1)
Remove a network
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBheliosctl\fR(1), for exit status, environment, files and security.
